# Backend i18n

- Client-facing text (errors, notifications, emails) uses **stable keys** (`errors.domain.code`) — **no hardcoded strings**
- Keys live in `packages/api` when part of contract shared with FE
- Locale detection order: `Accept-Language` (preferred) → `?lang=` → user preference (if logged in)
- Fallback to default locale (`en`) and **log warning** when translation key missing
- Validation messages use i18n keys (class-validator message key), not EN/VI literals
- Do **not** return raw Prisma/DB/internal messages to clients

